course: dictionary
lesson: 9681
title: Suddenly: change without warning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Suddenly» means quickly and without warning, when you did not expect it. It is an adverb, and its base is the adjective sudden. Writers use it to show a surprise or a turning point in a story.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Suddenly, the lights went out» tells you something happened fast and unexpectedly. To check your meaning, swap in «quickly and without warning». If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Other words and phrases do the same job, such as all of a sudden, in a flash, or without warning. A sudden storm or a sudden drop in temperature is one that arrives without warning.
fact: Suddenly means quickly and without warning.
fact: Sudden is the adjective: a sudden storm, a sudden stop.
fact: Phrases with a similar meaning are all of a sudden, in a flash, and without warning.
fact: «Suddenly» often signals a surprise or a turning point in a story.
fact: Sudden moves near animals can scare them, so move calmly around dogs and horses.
exercise: «Suddenly, the lights went out.» What does suddenly mean? | Very brightly | Again and again | Slowly and gently | *Quickly and without warning
exercise: «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» What does suddenly tell you about how flu starts? | It starts slowly over many weeks | *It starts quickly, with no warning | It never starts at all | It starts only in summer
exercise: «The sudden drop in temperature made everyone shiver.» Find and copy the adjective from the same family as suddenly. | everyone | drop | temperature | *sudden
test: «An old idea said the Indus cities were suddenly destroyed, but the decline was slow.» What does suddenly mean in this sentence? | Loudly | *Quickly, without warning | Happily | Very slowly, over many years
test: «Suddenly he throws down his brush and digs his way up into the sunshine.» Which phrase means the same as suddenly? | Once upon a time | *All of a sudden | Long ago | Very carefully
exam: «Suddenly he throws down his brush, says Hang spring-cleaning! and digs his way up into the sunshine.» What is the best meaning of suddenly? | *Quickly, with no warning | Carefully, after much thought | Angrily, over a long time | Happily and slowly
